// The game's 2D view, as a plane that fills the camera's vision.
//
// A 2D game in this engine is not a different renderer: it is the 3D one looking
// straight at a flat plane that exactly fills its view. Everything the game draws
// -- background, sprites, UI -- lands on that plane, and the camera never moves
// off it. That is why there is one pipeline and not two.
//
// When a plane exactly fills the view, the perspective divide cancels: every
// point maps to the same screen position it would have had with no camera at all,
// and the projection is an axis-aligned fit. So the plane is drawn here as that
// fit -- the game's logical rect, scaled to the panel, letterboxed to keep its
// aspect -- which is arithmetically the same picture as running it through
// d3_wtri and would only differ if the camera ever left the plane's normal.
//
// The letterbox is the same shape sys_fit computes for the window, and for the
// same reason: a 288x512 game in a 360x313 panel has to keep its proportions or
// the art is wrong in a way no game can compensate for.
//
// Where the plane lands is **not** computed here. ed_psc, ed_pl0 and ed_pt0 own
// it, because the picking code needs the same answer to turn a pointer position
// into an entity -- and a fit computed twice is a fit that disagrees with itself
// the moment one copy learns about the wheel. It did: zooming moved what was
// selectable and left the picture alone.
//
// Two clips, nested, and both are needed. The plane's furniture -- its
// background, its border -- is clipped to the **panel**, because a zoomed-in
// plane is larger than the panel. The game's own world is clipped to the
// **plane**, because a ground strip stretched twelve screens wide would otherwise
// run out across the letterbox: the game's screen is what it is drawing on, not
// the panel it happens to sit in.

ed_plane() {
  ed_clip_pane();
  ed_plane_at();
  sf_unclip();
} return void;

ed_plane3(int x, int y, int w, int h) {
  sf_rect(x, y, w, h, (import ed_gu)[1]);
  ed_pworld(x, y, w);
  ed_plane4(x, y, w, h);
} return void;
